---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import Message from "../../components/Message.astro"
import RailStep from "../../components/RailStep.astro"
import StreamPreview from "../../components/StreamPreview.astro"
import { currentApiVersion } from "../../lib/api-versions"
import "../../styles/quickstart.css"

const currentVersion = currentApiVersion()

const steps = [
  { id: "key", title: "Create an API key" },
  { id: "env", title: "Put it in your shell" },
  { id: "me", title: "Confirm who you are" },
  { id: "search", title: "Search what Threa remembers" },
]
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart · Threa Developers"
  description="Four steps from a new Threa API key to your first memo search, run from your own terminal."
  current="quickstart"
>
  <h1 id="quickstart">Quickstart.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Four steps from a new API key to searching what Threa remembers, run
    from your own terminal.
  </p>

  <section class="guide" data-guide aria-labelledby="quickstart">
    <div class="guide-bar" aria-hidden="true" data-decorative>
      <p class="guide-status" data-guide-status>
        Step 1 of 4: {steps[0].title}
      </p>
      <div class="guide-meter">
        {
          steps.map((s, i) => (
            <a class="gm-seg" href={`#step-${s.id}`} data-seg tabindex="-1" style={i === 0 ? "--fill: 1" : undefined}>
              <span class="gm-bar" />
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>

    <ol class="rail">
      <RailStep id="step-key" title={steps[0].title}>
        <p>
          In the app, open <strong>Workspace Settings → API Keys</strong>, create a
          personal access key, pick its scopes, and copy the
          <code>threa_uk_…</code> value. Threa shows it once and can't show
          it again.
        </p>
        <p>
          Give it <code>memos:read</code> for step 4. <code>GET /me</code> in
          step 3 takes no scope. Bot keys and the other scopes are in
          <a class="link" href="/developers/authentication">Authentication</a>.
        </p>
      </RailStep>

      <RailStep id="step-env" title={steps[1].title}>
        <p>
          Export the key and your workspace ID. The workspace ID is in the app
          URL, after <code>/w/</code>.
        </p>
        <CodeBlock
          lang="bash"
          label="Shell"
          code={`export THREA_API_KEY=threa_uk_...
export THREA_WORKSPACE_ID=ws_...`}
        />
      </RailStep>

      <RailStep id="step-me" title={steps[2].title}>
        <p>
          <code>GET /me</code> returns the identity behind the key. It's the
          quickest way to confirm a key is live and pointed at the right
          workspace.
        </p>
        <CodeBlock
          lang="bash"
          label="Who am I"
          code={`curl https://app.threa.io/api/v1/workspaces/$THREA_WORKSPACE_ID/me \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $THREA_API_KEY"`}
        />
        <div class="expect">
          <p class="expect-lead">
            A working key comes back as a <code>user</code> or a
            <code>bot</code> principal, with its API version:
          </p>
          <CodeBlock
            lang="json"
            label="200 response"
            code={`{
  "data": {
    "kind": "user",
    "workspaceId": "ws_...",
    "userId": "usr_...",
    "apiVersion": {
      "pinned": "${currentVersion}",
      "resolved": "${currentVersion}",
      "current": "${currentVersion}",
      "supported": ["${currentVersion}"]
    }
  }
}`}
          />
          <dl class="facts">
            <dt><code>user</code></dt>
            <dd>A personal access key. It acts as you, and messages it sends show as yours, flagged as sent via the API.</dd>
            <dt><code>bot</code></dt>
            <dd>A bot key. The bot acts as itself, in the streams it's been added to.</dd>
            <dt><code>401</code></dt>
            <dd>The key is missing or invalid.</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </RailStep>

      <RailStep id="step-search" title={steps[3].title}>
        <p>
          With <code>memos:read</code>, search memos the way Ariadne does.
          Search is semantic by default.
        </p>
        <CodeBlock
          lang="bash"
          label="Search memos"
          code={`curl -X POST https://app.threa.io/api/v1/workspaces/$THREA_WORKSPACE_ID/memos/search \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $THREA_API_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{ "query": "auth", "limit": 5 }'`}
        />
        <div class="expect">
          <p class="expect-lead">
            Each result is a memo: a title, an abstract, its knowledge type
            (a decision, a procedure, and so on), tags, and the ids of the
            messages it came from. It's the same memo Ariadne answers
            from in Threa:
          </p>
          <StreamPreview stream="platform">
            <Message author="maya" time="14:02">
              <div class="tl-text"><span class="mention">@ariadne</span> why did we pause the auth refactor?</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="ariadne" time="14:02">
              <div class="tl-text">It's on hold until Jordan's review of the token-rotation model.</div>
              <div class="recall-memo-card">
                <div class="rmc-icon"><svg><use href="#icon-compass" /></svg></div>
                <div class="rmc-body">
                  <div class="rmc-kicker"><span class="k-type">decision</span><span class="k-tag">#product</span></div>
                  <div class="rmc-title">Auth refactor held pending token-rotation review</div>
                </div>
                <div class="rmc-meta">Mar 12</div>
              </div>
            </Message>
          </StreamPreview>
          <p>
            Take a memo's <code>id</code> to
            <code>GET /memos/&#123;memoId&#125;</code> for the source stream and
            the exact messages, as in
            <a class="link" href="/developers/recipes#decisions">Find out what was decided, and why</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </RailStep>
    </ol>

    <div class="guide-next">
      <h2 id="next">Then pick a recipe</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="/developers/recipes#ci-notify">Notify a stream from CI</a>, with sends that never double-post on retry.</li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/developers/recipes#local-agent">Connect your local agent</a> so it replies in Threa.</li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/developers/reference">API reference</a> for every endpoint and its scope.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    import "../../scripts/guide.ts"
  </script>
</DocsLayout>
